title: What it actually cost, read from the bill
subtitle: week-14 — $0.6478 against a $1.74 prediction, and two meters that were invisible a day earlier
width: 1000
---
$ az rest --method post --url ".../Microsoft.CostManagement/query?api-version=2024-08-01" \
    --body '{"type":"ActualCost","timeframe":"Custom", ... }'

    0.4403  Azure Database for PostgreSQL
    0.1026  Virtual Machines
    0.0739  NAT Gateway
    0.0220  Virtual Network
    0.0073  Storage
    0.0016  Azure DNS
  --------
    0.6478  TOTAL

# Predicted BEFORE deploying, in meters.json: 1.74 for a three-hour window
# at 0.5808/hour. The resources existed 18:21Z - 19:36Z, one hour fifteen,
# which at those rates is about 0.73. The bill came in 11% under.
#
# The Virtual Network and Azure DNS rows are the private endpoint and the
# private DNS zone -- the two meters price_check.py could not see until the
# day before, one priced under region 'Global' and one on a bare "1" unit.
# Small, and not zero. A DNS Private Resolver sits on the same shelf at
# $180/month.
